          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best portable solar panel is the one that matches your station's input and your willingness to carry it. For most people that is the EcoFlow 220W Bifacial, which combines high output with an easy voltage, IP68 protection and a standard connector. Choose the SolarSaga 100W when weight matters, and the EcoFlow 400W when you need to refill a large station in a day.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, check Voc before the connector, plan on 70 percent of the rated watts, and keep panels in full sun at a sensible angle. Get those right and a portable panel will keep your station topped up for years.
          </p>
